#. FAQ answer explaining direct career-page indexing and no recruiter spam.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: app/[lang]/(public)/faq/page.tsx
msgid "faq.a.differentiation"
msgstr "We index company career pages directly, not third-party feeds. No recruiter spam, no reposted ghost jobs, and we re-check companies frequently — so most roles show up here within hours of being published. We're built for users who already know which companies they want to work at, not broad 'find me any job' searches."

#. FAQ answer accurately summarizing robots handling, request identity, pacing, and TDM policy.
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: app/[lang]/(public)/faq/page.tsx
msgid "faq.a.crawlingPolicy"
msgstr "We inspect robots.txt for sitemap discovery; Disallow enforcement is not yet active. We respect TDM-Reservation headers, pace requests per rate-limit domain, and use exponential backoff. Most requests use a stable browser-compatible User-Agent, while source-specific paths may use an identifying Job Seek UA. See our Job Indexing page for full details."

#. Step 1 body
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/HowWeIndexContent.tsx
msgid "indexing.ingestion.s1.body"
msgstr "We look for a sitemap that already lists every careers or job detail page—ideally linked from <0>robots.txt</0>—and rely on it whenever possible."

#. Ingestion section description
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
#: src/components/HowWeIndexContent.tsx
msgid "indexing.ingestion.description"
msgstr "We look for structured feeds before scraping raw HTML. First we check for sitemaps, then client-side JSON APIs, and only parse full pages when neither exists."

